{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md#2-per-project-setup-do-this-once-per-project-you-want-indexed","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md","heading":"2. Per-project setup (do this once per project you want indexed)","level":2,"anchor":"2-per-project-setup-do-this-once-per-project-you-want-indexed","span":{"start":61,"end":80},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:05410e011f5aaf3a120bdc3d296177625d3a8721841e9f13deeccf6b2049946c","meta":{"codeRefs":[".crib/","bash\ncd /path/to/your/project\ncrib index .                          # full index → .crib/ (the soul + derived sqlite index)\ncrib status .                         # confirm: nodes, edges, clusters, vcsHead","That's it. The","directory is the project's memory. **Commit","to git** so the whole\nteam (and every agent) shares the same soul — it's chunked JSONL, diff-friendly, and engine-free.","also **registers the project** in","(see §3) — a local pointer\ntable mapping this project's absolute path to its","cd","/path/to/your/project","crib","index","full","the","soul","derived","sqlite","status","confirm","nodes","edges","clusters","vcsHead"],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md#3-the-mcp-server-the-clients-connect-to","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md","heading":"3. The MCP server the clients connect to","level":2,"anchor":"3-the-mcp-server-the-clients-connect-to","span":{"start":130,"end":161},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:94d7a2519b85afe105638be2e554eb68a908c462841e0fb8d3e928a89b964797","meta":{"codeRefs":["crib serve <project-root>","The server speaks MCP over stdio, reads the soul from",", and exposes **17\ntools** (provenance-tagged + token-bounded so the agent never dumps the whole graph). The 11\nstructural tools:\n\n| Tool | What it returns |\n|---|---|\n|","| Health + node/edge/cluster counts + VCS anchor + capability flags |\n|","| Hybrid BM25 search over code + docs →",".","are BM25-ranked with a lightweight LLM pointer by default;","are semantic discoveries BM25 missed (separate, de-duped);","upgrades the pointer to the full analysis+graph+evidence blob |\n|","| 360° for one symbol: signature, callers, callees, linked docs |\n|","| Paged source body for a symbol (span rehydration) |\n|","| One-call deep context for a symbol: decision table, raises, handlers, cursors, declares, docs (persisted under",") |\n|","| Blast radius (up=dependents / down=dependencies) + docs |\n|","| Doc-sections linked to a symbol (cheap, high value) |\n|","| Raw adjacency (graph-walking primitive) |\n|","| Shortest directed path between two nodes |\n|","| Dry-run delta since a git ref (for reviewing diffs) |\n|","| Decision table from a procedure's guard-annotated CFG |\n\nPlus","(unimplemented symbols / missing package bodies / unresolved call sites) and the **5\nLLM-graph verbs** —",",","crib","serve","project","root"],"links":["knowledge-crib-user-guide.md#10-the-llm-semantic-graph-layer-the-grove-plan"]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md#4-claude-code","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md","heading":"4. Claude Code","level":2,"anchor":"4-claude-code","span":{"start":204,"end":255},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:2ce8ae380b2ded48b55e6cf7c550d2dd30ff561cb360a5c48ac624e63aca82df","meta":{"codeRefs":[".mcp.json","claude mcp add","json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"knowledge-crib\": {\n      \"command\": \"crib\",\n      \"args\": [\"serve\", \".\"]\n    }\n  }\n}","Then in that project:","will prompt you to approve the project MCP server on first use.\n\n**Option B — CLI (project-scope):**","bash\ncrib mcp install --ide claude              # writes .mcp.json with [\"serve\",\".\"] (committable)","**Option C — one user-scope entry for every project (recommended):**","bash\ncrib mcp install --ide claude --global     # runs","with","(no path)","The global entry runs","with **no path arg**, so the root-resolution chain in §3\n(","→ upward walk → registry) picks the right soul per workspace. One entry, every\nproject — no per-project config.\n\nVerify inside a Claude Code session:","/mcp          # lists connected servers + tools; knowledge-crib should show 17 tools (12 structural + 5 LLM-graph)","> The","in","is **not** resolved by Claude Code's CWD — Claude Code ignores the","field\n> (issue #42883). It works because","'s resolution chain falls through to","mcpServers","knowledge","crib","command","args","serve","mcp","install","ide","claude","writes","committable","global","runs","add","user","no","path","/mcp","lists","connected","servers","tools","should","show","17","12","structural","LLM","graph"],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md#5-cursor","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md","heading":"5. Cursor","level":2,"anchor":"5-cursor","span":{"start":256,"end":285},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:93be2127631ed58037991bd480e26163ddee1636a296ce32406c9bcd1806ed6a","meta":{"codeRefs":[".cursor/mcp.json","~/.cursor/mcp.json","bash\ncrib mcp install --ide cursor             # project: .cursor/mcp.json with ${workspaceFolder}\ncrib mcp install --ide cursor --global     # global: ~/.cursor/mcp.json (one entry, every project)","Or create","in the project root by hand:","json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"knowledge-crib\": {\n      \"command\": \"crib\",\n      \"args\": [\"serve\", \"${workspaceFolder}\"]\n    }\n  }\n}","Then **Reload Window** (","→ \"Reload Window\") and verify in\n**Settings → Tools & MCP** —","should show a green (connected) status. The MCP tools\nappear in Cursor's agent tool list.","crib","mcp","install","ide","cursor","project","with","workspaceFolder","global","/.cursor/mcp.json","one","entry","every","mcpServers","knowledge","command","args","serve"],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md#6-github-copilot-vs-code-ghcp","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md","heading":"6. GitHub Copilot (VS Code, \"ghcp\")","level":2,"anchor":"6-github-copilot-vs-code-ghcp","span":{"start":286,"end":319},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:648345d2412d0bb1984298ce14100085c74931e64a82ab212eb2f4a358d34cbf","meta":{"codeRefs":[".vscode/mcp.json","servers","mcpServers","type:\n\"stdio\"","bash\ncrib mcp install --ide vscode              # writes .vscode/mcp.json (servers + type:stdio)","> VS Code/Copilot user-scoped MCP config is not documented upstream, so only project-scope is\n> offered (the command notes + skips if you pass",").\n\nOr create","in the project root by hand (committable):","json\n{\n  \"servers\": {\n    \"knowledge-crib\": {\n      \"type\": \"stdio\",\n      \"command\": \"crib\",\n      \"args\": [\"serve\", \"${workspaceFolder}\"]\n    }\n  }\n}","Reload the VS Code window. In Copilot Chat, switch to **Agent mode** — the Knowledge-crib tools are\navailable. Verify in the Output panel (",") → \"MCP Logs\".\n\nCommon pitfall: using","here silently loads nothing — it must be","with","crib","mcp","install","ide","vscode","writes","type","stdio","knowledge","command","args","serve","workspaceFolder"],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md#7-openai-codex-cli","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-client-setup.md","heading":"7. OpenAI Codex CLI","level":2,"anchor":"7-openai-codex-cli","span":{"start":320,"end":359},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:97f148c42620058f20d6e7e71ac70d0360a633d7010aed6bd90c5aa0f60c1a6a","meta":{"codeRefs":["~/.codex/config.toml",".codex/config.toml","[mcp_servers.<name>]","[mcpServers]","[mcp.servers]","bash\ncrib mcp install --ide codex              # project: .codex/config.toml (managed TOML block)\ncrib mcp install --ide codex --global      # global: ~/.codex/config.toml","Or add to","by hand:","toml\n[mcp_servers.knowledge-crib]\ncommand = \"crib\"\nargs = [\"serve\", \"/absolute/path/to/project\"]\nstartup_timeout_sec = 20\ntool_timeout_sec = 60","Or via Codex CLI:","bash\ncodex mcp add knowledge-crib -- crib serve /absolute/path/to/project\ncodex mcp list                          # confirm it's registered","Inside the Codex TUI,","lists active servers and their tools.\n\n> **Honest limitation:** Codex does **not** interpolate",", so a Codex entry\n> must embed an absolute project path — one global Codex entry cannot transparently serve multiple\n> projects the way the Claude/Cursor user-scope entries can. Options: (a) one project-scoped\n>","per repo (committable, after marking the repo trusted), or (b) one global\n> entry per project in",". The","registry (§3) still resolves a custom\n>","location if the absolute path's","was moved, but it cannot make a single Codex\n> entry path-agnostic. This is the one IDE where the \"single entry for every project\" goal is not\n> fully achievable; the others reach it via","/","crib","mcp","install","ide","codex","project","managed","TOML","block","global","/.codex/config.toml","mcp_servers.knowledge","command","args","serve","/absolute/path/to/project","startup_timeout_sec","20","tool_timeout_sec","60","add","knowledge","list","confirm","it","registered"],"links":[]}}
